CORE
main.c
--32 --no-standard-checks
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ read before the object: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ in bounds: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
Invariant check failed
--
With a 32-bit size_t, the bound of the bytes to unpack (offset plus size,
computed in size_t) was 4294967292, and the lowering ran out of memory.
